      "lines": [
        "This chain is standing up. On its own."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hook",
      "pad_before": 0.15,
      "pad_after": 0.05,
      "min_duration": 3.3,
      "lines": [
        "Why does it do that? Watch. Bead chain, bucket, end over the rim."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obvious",
      "pad_before": 0.15,
      "pad_after": 0.5,
      "min_duration": 3.2,
      "lines": [
        "Pull the end, and obviously, it slides out."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "reversal",
      "pad_before": 0.2,
      "pad_after": 0.5,
      "min_duration": 7.0,
      "lines": [
        "But watch. It lifts itself out and floats above the rim. No hands. No trick. Until the bucket is empty. How?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "kick",
      "pad_before": 0.2,
      "pad_after": 0.45,
      "min_duration": 6.0,
      "lines": [
        "Each bead is a tiny rigid rod. When the chain yanks one end up, the other end kicks down into the pile. And the pile kicks back."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "equation",
      "pad_before": 0.2,
      "pad_after": 0.45,
      "min_duration": 6.0,
      "lines": [
        "That kick is a fraction, alpha, of the pull. Fountain height is alpha over one minus alpha, times the drop height. Alpha is about one eighth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scale",
      "pad_before": 0.2,
      "pad_after": 0.5,
      "min_duration": 5.0,
      "lines": [
        "Drop it one and a half meters, and it floats twenty centimeters above the rim. Drop it from a fourth floor balcony, and the fountain is as tall as you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cta",
      "pad_before": 0.15,
      "pad_after": 0.8,
      "min_duration": 2.6,
      "lines": [
        "Follow for more!"
      ]
    }
